## 12. 30-Day Speaking Practice Plan

> Follow this plan to go from **zero to basic fluency** in conversational Telugu.

---

### Week 1: Foundation (Days 1–7)
**Goal:** Understand the sounds and basic structure

| Day | Focus | Practice |
|-----|-------|---------|
| **Day 1** | Vowels + Numbers 1–10 | Say each vowel 5x aloud. Count to 10. |
| **Day 2** | Greetings (నమస్కారం, ఎలా ఉన్నావు, ధన్యవాదాలు) | Greet someone (or yourself in mirror) 10x |
| **Day 3** | "I am / I go / I eat" — Present tense only | Speak 5 sentences about yourself |
| **Day 4** | Filler words (కదా, అవును, లేదు, సరే, ఏమో) | Use them in 5 short replies |
| **Day 5** | "What? Where? When?" questions | Ask 5 questions about your surroundings |
| **Day 6** | Review all of Week 1 | Record yourself speaking 10 sentences |
| **Day 7** | Casual Dialogue 1 (Meeting a friend) | Read aloud 3x, then try without looking |

---

### Week 2: Past Tense (Days 8–14)
**Goal:** Talk about what happened today / yesterday

| Day | Focus | Practice |
|-----|-------|---------|
| **Day 8** | Past tense of 5 verbs (go, eat, come, see, do) | "I did X yesterday" — 5 sentences |
| **Day 9** | Negative past (didn't go, didn't eat) | Make each Day 8 sentence negative |
| **Day 10** | "He/She/They" in past tense | Describe what a friend did today |
| **Day 11** | Casual phrases: "I forgot", "What happened?" | Use them in 3 mini stories |
| **Day 12** | Slang + Filler words in sentences | Mix fillers into past tense sentences |
| **Day 13** | Dialogue 3 (Phone call) | Read aloud 3x, then improvise |
| **Day 14** | Review + Record yourself | Tell the story of your day in Telugu |

---

### Week 3: Future & Questions (Days 15–21)
**Goal:** Make plans and ask questions naturally

| Day | Focus | Practice |
|-----|-------|---------|
| **Day 15** | Future tense: "I will go, I will eat, I will come" | Plan tomorrow's day in Telugu aloud |
| **Day 16** | Question patterns (ఏం + verb, ఎక్కడ + verb) | Ask 10 different questions |
| **Day 17** | Yes/No questions (-వా? ending) | Convert 5 statements to questions |
| **Day 18** | "Can you? Will you? Shall we?" | Plan an outing in Telugu |
| **Day 19** | Emotion expressions | Describe how you felt about 3 events |
| **Day 20** | Dialogue 2 (Weekend plans) | Full spontaneous dialogue practice |
| **Day 21** | Review + Full story | Narrate a recent event (past → present → future) |

---

### Week 4: Fluency (Days 22–30)
**Goal:** Hold a real casual conversation for 5 minutes

| Day | Focus | Practice |
|-----|-------|---------|
| **Day 22** | Shopping + Food ordering | Role-play buying something |
| **Day 23** | WhatsApp-style messages (voice it aloud) | "Type" 10 messages, say them out loud |
| **Day 24** | Directions + Places | Describe how to get from home to a shop |
| **Day 25** | Tease / humor + Slang | Tell a mildly funny story in Telugu |
| **Day 26** | All dialogues end-to-end | Go through all 4 dialogues without stopping |
| **Day 27** | Shadow practice | Listen to a Telugu song / reel, try to mimic |
| **Day 28** | Describe your day fully in Telugu | 2 minutes of continuous speaking |
| **Day 29** | Have a real conversation | Talk to a Telugu speaker for 5 minutes |
| **Day 30** | Record yourself, compare to Day 1 | Celebrate your progress! 🎉 |

